{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1:_Pythagorean_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1: Pythagorean Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2:_Law_of_Cosines\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2: Law of Cosines</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3:_Stewart&#39;s_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3: Stewart's Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4:_Pappus&#39;s_Median_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4: Pappus's Median Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5:_Similar_Triangles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5: Similar Triangles</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a649aee592a9c37d2f9b5d5239f5e06e533130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/286e989082359d570543d0269004ce484008ce68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_of_a_triangle\" title=\"Median of a triangle\">median</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> have the same length. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01c54924155006184b7c28da19d141ff2409010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}2 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac 32 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"478\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1:_Pythagorean_Theorem\">Solution 1: Pythagorean Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1: Pythagorean Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/20552f4dac85af4806831750082aae9773f6b706.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  unitsize(4cm);  pair A, B, C, D, M;  A = (1.768,0.935); B = (1.414,0); C = (0,0); D = (1.768,0); M = (0.707,0);  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D); draw(D--B); draw(A--M);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,S); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(A+D)/2,E); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(B+D)/2,S); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(C+M)/2,S); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(M+B)/2,S); label(&quot;$2a$&quot;,(A+M)/2,SE); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(A+B)/2,SE); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(A+C)/2,NW);  draw(rightanglemark(B,D,A,3));  [/asy]\" width=\"365\" height=\"222\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> extended past <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc975a5b35343ca18565b3a7cce9827d332bbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85788f8dcf5ffb92327bf3a6751433064a5a6450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />.\nUsing the Pythagorean Theorem, we obtain the equations\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/8349c8156e4b5b1bffc9a5003fc3597575d9a704.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  x^2 + y^2 = 1 \\hspace{0.5cm}(1)\\\\ x^2 + y^2 + 2ya + a^2 = 4a^2 \\hspace{0.5cm}(2)\\\\ x^2 + y^2 + 4ya + 4a^2 = 4 \\hspace{0.5cm}(3) \\end{align*}\" width=\"242\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> equation from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2d2ff46f69061b7b7bd7f20a74d1c1adbbae08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2ya + a^2 = 4a^2 - 1 \\hspace{0.5cm}(4)\\\\ 4ya + 4a^2 = 3 \\hspace{0.5cm}(5) \\end{align*}\" width=\"194\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Then, subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf9b0d33251531e39f00dcb5dde9f96de857fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times (4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737a366a904e00f936f8728869ad8f2587dab46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and rearranging, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323737af46a15ea9df7570b0ff9e1743a78b096c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a^2 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5ff02f26f2b0fd8323a4a65dfe0e6b6eb6fcd4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2a = \\sqrt{2}\\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"187\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>~greenturtle 11/28/2017\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2:_Law_of_Cosines\">Solution 2: Law of Cosines</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2: Law of Cosines\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2002_12B_AMC-23.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/98/2002_12B_AMC-23.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"278\" height=\"121\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the median from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c9e0fdf79fc97acdc927584a47f082da0c13ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = BC = 2a$\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />. Then by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9119fa445a3201bfaa4eeb8bab4fb63ba4a15b3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD, \\triangle ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825119a3151ab7cbe20f9219217e9e0388e29b20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 1^2 &amp;= a^2 + (2a)^2 - 2(a)(2a)\\cos ADB \\\\ 2^2 &amp;= a^2 + (2a)^2 - 2(a)(2a)\\cos ADC  \\end{align*}\" width=\"281\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7a835092dad3bd2ae3bf04a6c52cf56931e780e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos ADC = \\cos (180 - ADB) = -\\cos ADB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />, we can add these two equations and get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7ef5bf2a35df8f95e354145fc0ffc141e39ae7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5 = 10a^2\\]\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/5230645e90ec7f6957a44a32a3be2d6421db2d5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"60\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3175e01d90a75b34b5da8687241cbd7bbcbdc2ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2a = \\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3:_Stewart.27s_Theorem\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3:_Stewart's_Theorem\">Solution 3: Stewart's Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3: Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">Stewart's Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88be3abe86be5ec685cab0597b12cbec10267176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)(1/2)a(2) + (1)(1/2)a(1) = (a)(a)(a) + (1/2)a(a)(1/2)a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"463\" height=\"18\" /> Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4b1da8b0fb1c2abd9c879d640b4fc1a16d330e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5/4)a^3 = (5/2)a \\implies (5/4)a^2 = 5/2 \\implies a^2 = 2 \\implies a = \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"515\" height=\"30\" />\n- awu2014\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4:_Pappus.27s_Median_Theorem\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4:_Pappus's_Median_Theorem\">Solution 4: Pappus's Median Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4: Pappus&#39;s Median Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There is a theorem in geometry known as Pappus's Median Theorem. It states that if you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, and you draw a median from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> (label this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />), then: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7a24ad1308ffeb7980afe91c95d5994709e2ac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AM)^2 = \\dfrac{2(b^2) + 2(c^2) - (a^2)}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"238\" height=\"41\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the length of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the length of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is length of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba748d16b1fd31ccc0c27ab9af73ea985b754ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB = MC = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3237f8499faf91a842140e269d551991a15a7d3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = 2x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />. Now, we can plug into the formula given above: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3237f8499faf91a842140e269d551991a15a7d3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = 2x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5351998230e216d9d0f2884c159326cfe6622263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/04643bfe42e5ea8b1ba453a3261f2ac9fb393800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. After some simple algebra, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e78104167925e390faab9f8b2e6da59c00e4026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"43\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fd437d03dfe2399a31dd61f68d0bd51d7e550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}} \\implies \\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"166\" height=\"32\" />. \n</p><p>-Flames\n</p><p>Note: Pappus's Median Theorem is just a special case of Stewart's Theorem, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39526a4fd8fa70a09be9251b26dbfb4bb423219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />. ~Puck_0\naka Apollonius' Theorem - Orion 2010\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5:_Similar_Triangles\">Solution 5: Similar Triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5: Similar Triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2002_12B_AMC-23.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/98/2002_12B_AMC-23.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"278\" height=\"121\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>First let us call the intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and the median <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff518de6defce08f1c1b44f73ef30205ac0595c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}:\\overline{AB}=2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191a971fd814314ba7c578811e1f8cbe249cf3a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MA}:\\overline{MB}=2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />, too. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fceead9fcbbf641c921e720250e42c7a62f0e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MBA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> share the same angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d089768b09c8f192985935b4efd1d34ab6094ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, we can say that the triangles have SSA similarity.\n</p><p>Technically, SSA similarity is invalid since there are two possible triangles which can be drawn with the same SSA. Just by looking at the diagram, we can tell that we have the correct triangle which is truly similar. If tried the same similarity with triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e066d23c76469a1b0be0b8a79e10a9eeecb747c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{MCA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, it would not work.\n</p><p>Now that we have similar triangles, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/30774361b95c0d3edb21dca88679b43594085a7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}:\\overline{BM}=\\overline{CB}:\\overline{BA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cae42b15a62d320f42bc20d6e9703d844ebcd59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:a=2a:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ed7fd314f2d644d1e2a41ec90cb6fc2ceb5909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734a2dee323036282ef1874cdcc70c6dadf3508a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />. Since the median has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90e35a9eab6930b55fece884d2014900c24c2bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}=\\boxed{\\sqrt2}\\implies \\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>-mathisfunsp\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jEVMgWKQIW8\">https://youtu.be/jEVMgWKQIW8</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B\">2002 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Precede